On Fri, Mar 12, 2010 at 1:07 PM, Michael Turniansky
<mturniansky@gmail.com> wrote:
>  If I say "To be or not to be" in the bathroom in the dead
> of night, that's still a bacru, but not a cusku.

You can still cusku something just to yourself though. A better
example of pure bacru might be some linguistic sound without any
meaning, like "ba be bi bo bu".

> Not all se bacru are
> se cusku, not all se cusku are se bacru.  But some are both.  The sets
> are not disjoint.

Right. I would say the relationship between them is something like:

ko'a bacru ko'e = ko'a cusku ko'e zi'o lo voksa

mu'o mi'e xorxes


